@startuml
title GET /api/wallets/{address}/state — balance and history readback
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Wallet holder" as Holder #FFD8C2
participant "WalletsApiSdk\n.getState()" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "WalletsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nread node" as Chain #FFE4A6

Holder -> SDK : getState()
SDK -> SDK : address = privateKey\n  .getPublicKey().getAddress()
SDK -> API : GET /api/wallets/{address}/state
API -> Domain : get_wallet_state_and_history(address)
Domain -> Chain : explore-deploy\nget_balance_and_history.rho\n(registry env URI, wallet address)
alt contract answers with state
  Chain --> Domain : { balance, transfers, boosts }
  Domain --> API : WalletStateAndHistory\n(exchanges: [], requests: [])
  API --> SDK : 200 WalletStateAndHistory
  SDK --> Holder : balance and history
else contract answers with an error
  Chain --> Domain : error string
  API <-- Domain : "error from contract: ..."
  SDK <-- API : 500 InternalError
end

note over Domain #FFF0C7
The read is an explore-deploy: it executes on the
read node without deploying anything and costs the
caller nothing. exchanges and requests are reserved
fields, currently always empty; history entries that
fail conversion are dropped from the response.
end note
@enduml
